{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Who perverts the justice of the stranger, the orphan.</b> For they have no helper, and indeed it too is in secret. And he mentioned the stranger, also the orphan and the widow, for if the judge perverts the justice of others, they will object against him and publicize him, but the stranger and the orphan and the widow have no power. And one who lies with a father's wife, or a sister, or a mother-in-law, is not suspected of secluding himself with her; therefore it is a hidden matter, and so it is not with the rest of the transgressions."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:02.878108248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}